<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating the pH, given the hydrogen ion concentration</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The pH of a solution is</p>
\[ \mathrm{pH} = -\log_{10}[\mathrm{H}^+], \]
<p>where \([\mathrm{H}^+]\) is the concentration of hydrogen ions in moles per litre (mol/L).</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> A sample of fruit juice has \([\mathrm{H}^+] = 10^{-{@p@}}\) mol/L. Find its pH.</p>
<p>pH \(=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> A sample of rainwater has \([\mathrm{H}^+] = {@a@} \times 10^{-{@n@}}\) mol/L. Find its pH to 2 decimal places.</p>
<p>pH \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> A solution has a pH of \({@q@}\). Find \([\mathrm{H}^+]\). You may type a power, such as <code>10^-4</code>, or a decimal.</p>
<p>\([\mathrm{H}^+] =\) [[input:ans3]] mol/L [[validation:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> \(\mathrm{pH} = -\log_{10} 10^{-{@p@}} = -(-{@p@}) = {@p@}\).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Use the product law, \(\log_{10}({@a@} \times 10^{-{@n@}}) = \log_{10} {@a@} + \log_{10} 10^{-{@n@}}\):</p>
\[ \mathrm{pH} = -\left(\log_{10} {@a@} - {@n@}\right) = {@n@} - \log_{10} {@a@} = {@n@} - {@float(log(a)/log(10))@}\ldots \approx {@ta2@}. \]
<p><strong>(c)</strong> \({@q@} = -\log_{10}[\mathrm{H}^+]\), so \(\log_{10}[\mathrm{H}^+] = -{@q@}\). In index form, \([\mathrm{H}^+] = 10^{-{@q@}}\) mol/L.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
